--- !u!114 &904476621
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 904476619}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UnityEngine.UI::UnityEngine.UI.Text
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 0.9}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 18
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 6
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 1
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "<b><size=18>Button guide</size></b>\n<color=#9fd8ff><b>Enter Area</b></color>
    \u2014 loads Island additively and restores any cubes from slot 1.\n<color=#9fd8ff><b>Spawn
    Cube</b></color> \u2014 instantiates a DemoCube INTO Island. Requires Island
    to be loaded.\n<color=#9fd8ff><b>Exit Area</b></color> \u2014 <b>auto-saves slot
    1 first</b>, then unloads Island. Cubes survive on disk.\n<color=#9fd8ff><b>Return
    To Area</b></color> \u2014 reloads Island. Does NOT save, so it will not overwrite
    your slot.\n<color=#9fd8ff><b>Save (slot 1)</b></color> \u2014 manual save. Use
    only while Island is loaded (see warnings below).\n<color=#9fd8ff><b>Load (slot
    1)</b></color> \u2014 deserializes slot 1 via the managed pipeline.\n<color=#9fd8ff><b>Delete
    Save</b></color> \u2014 wipes slot 1 so the next Enter Area starts empty.\n\n<b><size=18>Recommended
    flow</size></b>\n1) Enter Area  \u2192  2) Spawn Cube (one or more)  \u2192 
    3) Exit Area (auto-saves)  \u2192  4) Return To Area\n\n<b><size=18>Persistence
    across Play Mode</size></b>\nSlot 1 lives on disk. Leaving Play Mode keeps it.
    Re-enter Play and click Enter Area to see\nyour cubes again. Use <b>Delete Save</b>
    to start fresh.\n\n<b><size=18>Pitfalls</size></b>\n<color=#ffb36b>\u2022</color>
    Do NOT click <b>Save</b> right after <b>Exit Area</b>. Exit already saved; saving
    with Island\n   unloaded overwrites the slot with only the boot scene's contents,
    losing your Island cubes.\n<color=#ffb36b>\u2022</color> <b>Spawn Cube</b> only
    works while Island is loaded. Click Enter Area first."
